ce. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete and coherent: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, an observed outage, a different boot identity, recovered services/network/storage, persistent controls, and a successful post-restart crash test. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart. Task functionality is strong, though hygiene is reduced by the unrelated retained SSH repair.","limitations":["The controlled crash used www-data under systemd. Other active service accounts were directly inspected for 0/0 limits but were not each crash-tested; the PAM path was limit-checked rather than crash-tested.","Crash logging evidence consists of systemd/journald signal and exit metadata; no coredumpctl record was available.","Lifecycle snapshots do not directly inventory the generated SSH key files, although SSH remaining active after restart shows that the repair persisted."]}
